# Exam track — Theme: Akafe Goen (Going Shopping) — Sub-lesson 3: Talking About It
# @question sentences: the examiner asks in Luxembourgish, the learner
# assembles the Luxembourgish answer (always en→lu).
# Question words and connectors are drilled as vocabulary alongside them.
#
# The answers are the user's own (collected in an interview 2026-08-11), so the
# learner rehearses their real exam answers, not generic ones.

@lesson S1.03 "Talking About Shopping"

@word wéi vill = how much
@word wéini = when
@word wou = where
@word wéi = how
@word firwat = why
@word de Frigo = the fridge
@word d'Tankstell = the petrol station
@word d'Bicher = the books
@word d'Kleeder = the clothes
@word den Handy = the mobile phone
@word ronn = about
@word seelen = rarely
@word no der Aarbecht = after work
@word an der Woch = per week

@sentence
@question Wou gitt Dir akafen?
@lu Ech ginn am Cactus akafen, dee ass no bei mir.
@en I shop at Cactus, it is near me.
@distractor-lu wäit
@distractor-lu Maart

@sentence
@question Wéini gitt Dir akafen?
@lu Ech ginn no der Aarbecht owes akafen.
@en I go shopping in the evening after work.
@distractor-lu moies
@distractor-lu Samschdeg

@sentence
@question Wéi bezuelt Dir am léifsten?
@lu Ech bezuelen am léifste mat der Kaart.
@en I prefer to pay by card.
@distractor-lu Geld
@distractor-lu ni

@sentence
@question Wat kaaft Dir dacks?
@lu Ech kafen dacks Mëllech, Kéis a Fleesch.
@en I often buy milk, cheese and meat.
@distractor-lu Uebst
@distractor-lu seelen

@sentence
@question Gitt Dir eleng akafen?
@lu Nee, ech gi mat menger Famill akafen.
@en No, I go shopping with my family.
@distractor-lu eleng
@distractor-lu jo

@sentence
@question Maacht Dir eng Lëscht virdrun?
@lu Nee, ech kucke just an de Frigo.
@en No, I just look in the fridge.
@distractor-lu Lëscht
@distractor-lu schreiwen

@sentence
@question Gitt Dir gär akafen?
@lu Nee, dat dauert ze laang fir mech.
@en No, that takes too long for me.
@distractor-lu gär
@distractor-lu kuerz

@sentence
@question Kaaft Dir och online?
@lu Jo, ech kafe Kleeder a Bicher online.
@en Yes, I buy clothes and books online.
@distractor-lu Iesswueren
@distractor-lu nee

@sentence
@question Wéi vill bezuelt Dir an der Woch?
@lu Ech bezuele ronn honnert Euro an der Woch.
@en I pay about one hundred euros per week.
@distractor-lu Mount
@distractor-lu fofzeg

@sentence
@question Kucke Dir op d'Präisser?
@lu Just bei deiere Saache kucken ech op de Präis.
@en I only look at the price for expensive things.
@distractor-lu bëllege
@distractor-lu ëmmer

@sentence
@question Gitt Dir op de Maart?
@lu Seelen, ech hunn net vill Zäit.
@en Rarely, I do not have much time.
@distractor-lu dacks
@distractor-lu Geld

@sentence
@question Wat maacht Dir, wann e Buttek zou ass?
@lu Da ginn ech an d'Tankstell, do ass ëmmer op.
@en Then I go to the petrol station, it is always open.
@distractor-lu zou
@distractor-lu Bäckerei
